00:04:39.956 --> 00:04:42.958
- It is a newspaper, but my
Mom sent it to me on Facebook.

00:04:42.958 --> 00:04:43.733
- Amazing.

00:04:43.733 --> 00:04:47.270
- So, it was called 'No
Time To Be Nice At Work'

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.601
and it was all about how
the workplace is becoming

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.883
a hostile environment now
because people aren't civil

00:04:52.883 --> 00:04:55.930
to one another because of a
bunch of external factors.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.699
They're focused on a bunch
of other different things.

00:04:57.699 --> 00:04:58.391
- Like what?

00:04:58.391 --> 00:04:59.575
- So people aren't nice to each other

00:04:59.575 --> 00:05:03.965
because the pressure of day-to-day tasks,

00:05:03.965 --> 00:05:05.368
they're thinking about something else

00:05:05.368 --> 00:05:07.102
when they're in a
conversation with somebody.

00:05:07.102 --> 00:05:07.655
- OK.

00:05:07.655 --> 00:05:08.734
- How do you find--

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:09.675
- What was the point of the article,

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:10.987
like what was it trying to say?

00:05:10.987 --> 00:05:12.793
- It was trying to say that

00:05:12.793 --> 00:05:14.227
there's always time to kind of like

00:05:14.227 --> 00:05:17.536
take a deep breath and say
hi, how are you, to somebody,

00:05:17.536 --> 00:05:19.229
which I think you do a really good job of.

00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:19.972
- Okay.

00:05:19.972 --> 00:05:22.949
- So how do you find the time to focus?

00:05:22.949 --> 00:05:24.187
We're having a conversation right now,

00:05:24.187 --> 00:05:27.758
this is a great example,
but how do you find the time

00:05:27.758 --> 00:05:31.365
to focus, be nice to
people, stay in the moment,

00:05:31.365 --> 00:05:32.353
that kind of thing?

00:05:32.353 --> 00:05:33.090
- How do I personally?

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:34.595
- Yes, you personally.

00:05:36.065 --> 00:05:38.965
- You know I don't think I
really have any other gear.

00:05:38.965 --> 00:05:40.671
I truly believe like DNA

00:05:40.671 --> 00:05:42.862
and the way you were brought up is real.

00:05:42.862 --> 00:05:44.211
I truly look around this room

00:05:44.211 --> 00:05:46.847
and there's different levels
of being a nice person

00:05:46.847 --> 00:05:48.678
in this room, it's just real.

00:05:48.678 --> 00:05:50.832
It's just a real thing, right?

00:05:50.832 --> 00:05:52.528
For me, it's super easy.

00:05:52.528 --> 00:05:54.670
So here's what I would say,
I think that one thing I like

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:59.670
to say a lot is money and
micro-fame or real fame

00:05:59.965 --> 00:06:02.792
doesn't change a person,
it just exposes a person.

00:06:02.792 --> 00:06:04.911
So the amount of people
that write me emails

00:06:04.911 --> 00:06:07.509
or see me in the street like,
"wow you're...", they'll like

00:06:07.509 --> 00:06:10.062
send a tweet after they take
a selfie with me in the street

00:06:10.062 --> 00:06:12.549
and they're like, "Wow, Gary
Vee's a really nice guy!"

00:06:12.549 --> 00:06:16.624
Like, you actually get credit
for being a nice person

00:06:16.624 --> 00:06:18.342
the more exposure you get.

00:06:18.342 --> 00:06:19.770
Which I think is silly.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:22.545
Which I think is kind of
just a weird kind of dynamic.

00:06:22.545 --> 00:06:25.261
So, I think that falls in the
same realm as your question

00:06:25.261 --> 00:06:28.489
which is, you know, I
don't think external things

00:06:28.489 --> 00:06:30.324
in the world, like 24/7 world,

00:06:30.324 --> 00:06:32.064
I don't think anything's really changed.

00:06:32.064 --> 00:06:35.011
I don't think Gertrude is nicer or meaner

00:06:35.011 --> 00:06:38.851
because it's 2013 and
not 1955 anymore, right?

00:06:38.851 --> 00:06:41.318
I really don't think that, I
just think Gertrude's a (beep)

00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.640
and like decided not to be nice

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.626
just like she wouldn't have
been nice 30 years ago.

00:06:44.626 --> 00:06:48.027
And so, for me, I don't
even know any other Gary.

00:06:48.027 --> 00:06:49.782
As a matter of fact, I'm
probably a little bit weird

00:06:49.782 --> 00:06:53.848
the other way, which
is I'm so uncomfortable

00:06:53.848 --> 00:06:57.347
with negativity and angst,
things of that nature,

00:06:57.347 --> 00:06:58.707
that I attack it in reverse.

00:06:58.707 --> 00:07:00.959
A lot of my day is taken up trying

00:07:00.959 --> 00:07:03.466
to make sure that's
contained and not happening.

00:07:03.466 --> 00:07:04.941
So, it's just my default.

00:07:04.941 --> 00:07:06.462
I think there's a lot of value in it.

00:07:06.462 --> 00:07:08.958
I'm stunned how many people undervalue

00:07:08.958 --> 00:07:10.838
a head-nod or a "hey".

00:07:10.838 --> 00:07:13.357
For me, because as you guys
know I'm running around so much,

00:07:13.357 --> 00:07:17.071
so much of my stuff is like
a wink or a smile or a,

00:07:17.071 --> 00:07:20.606
it's just I don't have the
time, but it's so nice.

00:07:20.624 --> 00:07:24.915
I think people really
value effort, and intent.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.498
And I think you can get away with doing

00:07:26.498 --> 00:07:30.362
so much of that stuff, with
such little stuff, right?

00:07:30.362 --> 00:07:34.264
And so, for me it's easy
because my parents had sex

00:07:34.264 --> 00:07:36.821
at the right moment to give me my DNA.

00:07:36.821 --> 00:07:37.760
- [Kim] (applause)

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:38.375
- Thank you, Kim.

00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:40.058
And,
- (laughter)

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:43.518
and my Mom really parented me in a way

00:07:43.518 --> 00:07:44.980
to really value other people

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.501
and all that kind of stuff.

00:07:46.501 --> 00:07:48.683
And so, I just haven't
known any different.

00:07:49.253 --> 00:07:52.061
I love that I get like extra
credit for it now-a-days

00:07:52.061 --> 00:07:54.442
because a couple people
follow me on social media.

00:07:54.442 --> 00:07:55.660
But, for me there's, ya know,

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.859
and more importantly, and I
think you know this, and I think

00:07:58.859 --> 00:08:00.919
a lot of you know this and
some of you don't know this,

00:08:00.919 --> 00:08:03.759
but it's what's more interesting
to me is I believe in it

00:08:03.759 --> 00:08:07.281
so much the level of which
I'm forcing it down below me,

00:08:07.281 --> 00:08:09.718
not just leading by example
but being pretty upfront

00:08:09.718 --> 00:08:12.354
with senior leadership of
how much it matters to me

00:08:12.354 --> 00:08:15.346
is I think helps our company.

00:08:15.346 --> 00:08:15.919
- For sure.

00:08:15.919 --> 00:08:16.831
- Cool.
- It does.

00:08:16.831 --> 00:08:18.061
- Thanks Mol.

00:08:18.061 --> 00:08:21.169
- [Group] (applause)

00:08:21.874 --> 00:08:22.397
- How are you brother?
- Good, how about yourself?

00:08:22.397 --> 00:08:23.139
